# Lab 03: Working with AMI and EBS

## Objective
In this lab, I worked with EC2, AMIs and EBS to learn how to copy an EC2 setup to another AWS region and manage additional storage.

## 1. Launch EC2 in N. Virginia
I launched a Linux EC2 instance in the N. Virginia region (`us-east-1`).

[Paste screenshot]

## 2. Create an AMI
I created an AMI from the instance. This gave me a reusable image of the EC2 setup.

[Paste screenshot]

## 3. Copy to Oregon
I copied the AMI to the Oregon region (`us-west-2`) and used it to launch another instance with the same setup.

[Paste screenshot]

## 4. Add EBS Storage
Back in N. Virginia, I created two EBS volumes and attached them to my EC2 instance as additional storage.

[Paste screenshot]

## 5. Remove One Volume
I detached one of the additional EBS volumes and deleted it.

[Paste screenshot]

## 6. Increase the Storage
I increased the size of the second EBS volume to practice modifying storage without creating a new volume.

[Paste screenshot]

## 7. Back Up the Volume
Finally, I created a snapshot of the remaining EBS volume as a backup.

[Paste screenshot]

## What I Learned
This lab helped me understand the difference between an AMI and EBS storage. I also practiced copying an EC2 setup between regions, adding and modifying storage, and creating an EBS backup.
